From 212c2d88cf61b61678ff438b54d52948a266b7a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Przemyslaw Nogaj <pno@spyro-soft.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:06:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rhi: Track a pass's resources without keeping them sorted

QRhiPassResourceTracker kept the buffers and textures of a pass in a
QVarLengthFlatMap, which inserts by shifting everything after the new
key. That is quadratic in the number of resources in the pass, and a
pass can track thousands, such as the vertex and index buffers of
thousands of draw calls. How often that happens depends on the backend:
Vulkan only tracks a resource when its usage state changes, for example
after an upload, while OpenGL tracks every buffer a draw call uses, in
every frame. In a Qt Quick 3D scene of about 2900 draw calls per frame
on OpenGL, the shadow and depth passes spent half of the render
thread's time in those shifts.

Keep the resources in the order the pass first used them instead,
search them linearly while there are few, and index them by key once
there are more. Nothing depended on the order.

Amends 0e51db1eb51d15463b70e35fcdda772594e63aac.

Fixes: QTBUG-150982
Change-Id: I935ea6f8190f8c3e2ab3c02e88f74312a5ee9623
Reviewed-by: Laszlo Agocs <laszlo.agocs@qt.io>
(cherry picked from commit e333955c25b90d3b90ccc06ce7db8a6417c45d06)
---
 src/gui/rhi/qrhi.cpp       |  4 +-
 src/gui/rhi/qrhi_p.h       | 80 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/gui/rhi/qrhivulkan_p.h |  2 +
 3 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gui/rhi/qrhi.cpp b/src/gui/rhi/qrhi.cpp
